1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,585
Five teams.

2
00:00:02,655 --> 00:00:05,567
One task: a presentation due on Friday.

3
00:00:05,637 --> 00:00:08,162
Same deadline, very different stories.

4
00:00:08,232 --> 00:00:09,443
Which team are you in?

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,585
Anna: Okay team, it's Monday.

6
00:00:14,455 --> 00:00:15,713
Anna: I made a plan.

7
00:00:15,583 --> 00:00:16,890
Anna: Ben, research.

8
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:18,139
Anna: Chloe, slides.

9
00:00:18,009 --> 00:00:19,477
Anna: I'll write the script.

10
00:00:19,507 --> 00:00:20,953
Ben: Done by Wednesday.

11
00:00:20,983 --> 00:00:22,619
Chloe: I'll send a draft tonight.

12
00:00:22,649 --> 00:00:23,909
The Productive Team.

13
00:00:23,979 --> 00:00:26,142
Clear roles, clear deadlines.

14
00:00:26,212 --> 00:00:29,234
They finished on Wednesday and spent Friday relaxing.

15
00:00:29,304 --> 00:00:30,632
Result: A.

16
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:35,661
Dan: The background should be blue!

17
00:00:35,691 --> 00:00:37,111
Emma: No, green!

18
00:00:36,981 --> 00:00:38,278
Emma: Blue is boring!

19
00:00:38,308 --> 00:00:41,190
Finn: Guys… we haven't even picked a topic yet.

20
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:42,547
Dan & Emma: STAY OUT OF THIS!

21
00:00:42,577 --> 00:00:43,761
The Argument Team.

22
00:00:43,831 --> 00:00:46,189
Full of passion, zero progress.

23
00:00:46,259 --> 00:00:48,271
Three days of debate about colors.

24
00:00:48,341 --> 00:00:51,416
Result: a very beautiful empty slide.

25
00:00:54,567 --> 00:00:56,145
Gina: Should we start the project?

26
00:00:56,175 --> 00:00:56,754
Hugo: Nah.

27
00:00:56,624 --> 00:00:58,009
Hugo: We still have time.

28
00:00:58,039 --> 00:00:59,493
Ivy: Yeah, tomorrow.

29
00:01:00,703 --> 00:01:01,608
Gina: Guys.

30
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:02,858
Gina: It's due TOMORROW.

31
00:01:02,888 --> 00:01:03,643
Hugo & Ivy: WHAT?!

32
00:01:03,673 --> 00:01:04,874
The "Later" Team.

33
00:01:04,944 --> 00:01:07,422
Relaxed all week, panicked all night.

34
00:01:07,492 --> 00:01:10,566
Result: twelve slides, zero sleep.

35
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:15,684
Jake: Okay, meeting starts now.

36
00:01:15,554 --> 00:01:17,456
Jake: First… who wants pizza?

37
00:01:17,486 --> 00:01:18,323
Kim: Me!

38
00:01:18,193 --> 00:01:20,724
Kim: Wait, did anyone watch that new movie?

39
00:01:20,754 --> 00:01:23,368
Leo: Oh, I have a funny video to show you!

40
00:01:23,398 --> 00:01:24,379
The Fun Team.

41
00:01:24,449 --> 00:01:27,984
Best friendships, best snacks, worst productivity.

42
00:01:28,054 --> 00:01:30,231
Five meetings, zero slides.

43
00:01:30,301 --> 00:01:32,068
But hey, they had a great time.

44
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:37,625
Mia: I think blue is better, but let's vote.

45
00:01:37,655 --> 00:01:38,823
Noah: Fine with me.

46
00:01:38,693 --> 00:01:40,272
Noah: Break after this part?

47
00:01:40,142 --> 00:01:41,424
Noah: I brought snacks.

48
00:01:41,454 --> 00:01:42,212
Olivia: Deal.

49
00:01:42,082 --> 00:01:43,798
Olivia: Let's finish by Thursday.

50
00:01:43,828 --> 00:01:44,990
The Balanced Team.

51
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:50,511
They plan like the Productive Team, have fun like the Fun Team, and disagree without fighting.

52
00:01:53,667 --> 00:01:56,020
The best team isn't the smartest one.

53
00:01:56,090 --> 00:02:00,465
It's the one that communicates, plans, and still knows how to have fun.

54
00:02:00,535 --> 00:02:01,983
So, which team are you in?

55
00:02:02,053 --> 00:02:03,414
Tell us in the comments.
